<!-- Explainer v2 reference sample: all eight snippets plus a toggle, a slider
     over three precomputed SVG frames, and a step-through. Rendered by hand in
     the view to check both themes; not read by any test runner. -->
<p>The engine moves every player once per tick. A tick reads the ball, picks an
action for each player, and writes the new positions. This page shows how a
tick runs, where its parts sit on screen, and why the budget is 16 ms.</p>

<p>First, the order of work inside one tick.</p>
<!-- @include explainer/sequence {"title": "One tick, in order",
     "steps": [
       {"label": "Read the ball", "lane": "engine", "text": "Position and speed from the last tick."},
       {"label": "Pick actions", "lane": "AI", "text": "Each player scores its options."},
       {"label": "Write positions", "lane": "engine", "text": "One pass, no allocation."}
     ]} -->
<p>The engine owns the first and last step; the AI owns only the choice.</p>

<p>The same flow, one step at a time.</p>
<!-- @include explainer/steps {"title": "Walk through a tick",
     "steps": [
       {"label": "Read the ball", "text": "The engine copies the ball state so the AI reads a stable value."},
       {"label": "Score options", "text": "Each player rates pass, run and shoot from 0 to 1.", "tone": "warn"},
       {"label": "Resolve clashes", "text": "Two players who want the same space: the nearer one wins.", "tone": "risk"},
       {"label": "Write positions", "text": "All players move at once, so order does not matter.", "tone": "ok"}
     ]} -->

<p>Where each part sits on the match screen.</p>
<!-- @include explainer/layout {"title": "Match screen", "cols": 4, "rows": 3,
     "regions": [
       {"label": "Score bar", "col": 1, "row": 1, "w": 4, "tone": "muted"},
       {"label": "Pitch", "col": 1, "row": 2, "w": 3, "h": 2, "tone": "ok", "note": "redrawn every tick"},
       {"label": "Events", "col": 4, "row": 2, "tone": "accent", "note": "goals, cards"},
       {"label": "Controls", "col": 4, "row": 3, "tone": "warn"}
     ],
     "caption": "The pitch keeps three quarters of the width."} -->
<p>The pitch is the only region that changes every tick. The score bar and the
event list change only when a goal or a card happens, so they skip most redraws.</p>

<p>How the tick time changed as the AI grew.</p>
<!-- @include explainer/trend {"title": "Tick time per build", "unit": "ms",
     "x": ["b1", "b2", "b3", "b4", "b5", "b6"],
     "series": [
       {"label": "Mean", "values": [6, 7, 9, 12, 10, 8], "tone": "accent"},
       {"label": "p95", "values": [9, 11, 14, 19, 15, 12], "tone": "bad"}
     ]} -->
<p>Build b4 added a deeper search and the slow ticks went over budget. Builds b5
and b6 cut the search back, and the p95 line fell under 16 ms again.</p>

<p>Where the time goes in one tick.</p>
<!-- @include explainer/comparison {"title": "Time per part", "unit": "ms", "max": 16,
     "bars": [
       {"label": "Read", "value": 1, "tone": "muted"},
       {"label": "AI", "value": 9, "tone": "warn", "note": "the part to watch"},
       {"label": "Write", "value": 2, "tone": "ok"}
     ]} -->
<p>The AI takes more than half of the budget. Reading and writing are cheap, so
any saving must come from the decide step.</p>

<p>A player's states during a match.</p>
<!-- @include explainer/states {"title": "Player state",
     "states": [
       {"id": "idle", "label": "Idle"},
       {"id": "run", "label": "Running", "tone": "ok"},
       {"id": "tackle", "label": "Tackling", "tone": "warn"},
       {"id": "hurt", "label": "Injured", "tone": "bad", "note": "leaves the pitch after 3 ticks"}
     ],
     "transitions": [
       {"from": "idle", "to": "run", "label": "ball near"},
       {"from": "run", "to": "tackle", "label": "in reach"},
       {"from": "tackle", "to": "run", "label": "won"},
       {"from": "tackle", "to": "hurt", "label": "foul"},
       {"from": "run", "to": "run", "label": "chase"}
     ]} -->
<p>An injured player stays on the pitch for three ticks, then leaves. The tackle
state is the only way into the injured state.</p>

<p>The loop the engine repeats until the whistle.</p>
<!-- @include explainer/cycle {"title": "Tick loop",
     "states": [{"label": "Read"}, {"label": "Decide", "tone": "warn"}, {"label": "Move", "tone": "ok"}, {"label": "Render", "tone": "muted"}]} -->

<p>Which module calls which.</p>
<!-- @include explainer/dependency {"title": "Modules",
     "nodes": [{"id": "ui", "label": "Match screen"}, {"id": "eng", "label": "Engine"}, {"id": "ai", "label": "Player AI", "tone": "warn"}],
     "edges": [{"from": "ui", "to": "eng", "label": "tick()"}, {"from": "eng", "to": "ai", "label": "decide()"}]} -->

<p>Before and after the budget change. Press a button to switch.</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:10px 0">
  <button data-ex-toggle="budget" data-ex-show="before">Before</button>
  <button data-ex-toggle="budget" data-ex-show="after">After</button>
</div>
<div data-ex-panel="budget" data-ex-key="before">
<!-- @include explainer/comparison {"title": "Before: 24 ms budget", "unit": "ms", "max": 24,
     "bars": [{"label": "AI", "value": 18, "tone": "bad"}, {"label": "Rest", "value": 6, "tone": "muted"}]} -->
</div>
<div data-ex-panel="budget" data-ex-key="after">
<!-- @include explainer/comparison {"title": "After: 16 ms budget", "unit": "ms", "max": 24,
     "bars": [{"label": "AI", "value": 9, "tone": "ok"}, {"label": "Rest", "value": 3, "tone": "muted"}]} -->
</div>

<p>How the AI search depth changes the tick time. Move the slider.</p>
<label style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:14px;color:var(--ink-2)">Search depth
  <input type="range" data-ex-slider="depth" min="1" max="3" step="1" value="2">
  <b data-ex-value="depth" data-ex-unit="levels" style="color:var(--ink)">2 levels</b>
</label>
<div data-ex-frames="depth">
  <svg data-ex-frame="1" viewBox="0 0 320 120" width="100%" style="max-width:320px;display:block" role="img" aria-labelledby="dep1-t">
    <title id="dep1-t">Depth 1: 4 ms, well under the 16 ms budget</title>
    <line x1="10" x2="310" y1="30" y2="30" style="stroke:var(--high);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/>
    <text x="310" y="24" text-anchor="end" style="fill:var(--high);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px">budget 16 ms</text>
    <rect x="10" y="90" width="75" height="20" style="fill:var(--low)"/>
    <text x="92" y="105" style="fill:var(--ink);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px">4 ms</text>
  </svg>
  <svg data-ex-frame="2" viewBox="0 0 320 120" width="100%" style="max-width:320px;display:block" role="img" aria-labelledby="dep2-t">
    <title id="dep2-t">Depth 2: 9 ms, under the 16 ms budget</title>
    <line x1="10" x2="310" y1="30" y2="30" style="stroke:var(--high);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/>
    <text x="310" y="24" text-anchor="end" style="fill:var(--high);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px">budget 16 ms</text>
    <rect x="10" y="90" width="169" height="20" style="fill:var(--med)"/>
    <text x="186" y="105" style="fill:var(--ink);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px">9 ms</text>
  </svg>
  <svg data-ex-frame="3" viewBox="0 0 320 120" width="100%" style="max-width:320px;display:block" role="img" aria-labelledby="dep3-t">
    <title id="dep3-t">Depth 3: 21 ms, over the 16 ms budget</title>
    <line x1="10" x2="310" y1="30" y2="30" style="stroke:var(--high);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/>
    <text x="310" y="24" text-anchor="end" style="fill:var(--high);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px">budget 16 ms</text>
    <rect x="10" y="90" width="240" height="20" style="fill:var(--high)"/>
    <text x="256" y="105" style="fill:var(--ink);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px">21 ms</text>
  </svg>
</div>

<h3>Recap</h3>
<ul>
  <li>A tick reads, decides, then writes; only the decide step belongs to the AI.</li>
  <li>The AI is most of the tick, so its search depth sets the budget.</li>
  <li>Depth 2 is the deepest search that fits in 16 ms.</li>
</ul>
